From 57cc7c097c4c381b6724251c8afe765068590e3f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 22:39:03 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] udev buttonmaps for the Xbox and DualShock 4 controllers that
 Linux 7.2 defines

The add-on uses its udev driver on Linux by default, and a buttonmap is
used only for a controller with its exact name, vid/pid and counts of
buttons and axes. Several common controllers had none, so Kodi did not
react to them until the user mapped them by hand, and the d-pad of the
Xbox 360 wireless receiver was wrong.

These maps follow from what the kernel drivers set up, which defines the
input device in full for these controllers: xpad (Xbox pads over USB and
the Xbox 360 wireless receiver) and hid-playstation (DualShock 4). The udev
driver numbers the buttons by key code and the axes by ABS code, and the
same model gives, byte for byte, the maps of the add-on made with real
controllers (DualShock 4 and DualSense over USB, the Steam Xbox 360 pad,
the Xbox One pad of 2015, and the 360 wireless receiver as it was).

New:
- Microsoft X-Box 360 pad (045E:028E);
- Xbox 360 Wireless Receiver (the official receiver; xpad gives its pads
  the product 02A1);
- Microsoft X-Box One pad (02D1) and One S pad (02EA);
- Microsoft X-Box One Elite pad (02E3) and Elite 2 pad (0B00): their four
  paddles are buttons after the others, left unmapped;
- Microsoft Xbox Series S|X Controller (0B12): its share button is
  KEY_RECORD, the lowest key code, so every other button is one higher
  than on the One pads;
- the DualShock 4 over Bluetooth ("Wireless Controller", 054C:09CC and
  05C4) and the first DualShock 4 over USB ("Sony Computer Entertainment
  Wireless Controller", 05C4).

The triggers of these pads rest at the minimum of their range, so the maps
say so (center -1, range 2), as the add-on's Xbox 360 maps do.

Corrected: Xbox 360 Wireless Receiver (XBOX), 0291 and 02A1. Its d-pad was
mapped when xpad gave it as BTN_TRIGGER_HAPPY1 to 4 (left, right, up,
down); xpad now gives BTN_DPAD_UP, DOWN, LEFT and RIGHT, which sort in that
order, so up moved Kodi left, down right, left up and right down.

Not here: Xbox controllers over Bluetooth, whose buttons come from the
report descriptor of each firmware (hid-generic), and other makers' pads.
